the senate may not be able to meet its  self-imposed deadline to finalize its  details for a bipartisan gun reform deal  10 democrats and 10 republicans  announced a compromise package last week  to curb gun violence in the wake of  recent mass shootings but after several  meetings this week lawmakers are still  at odds mainly over two provisions  including what's known as the boyfriend  loophole that prevents domestic abusers  from owning guns christina raffini is at  the white house with more christina good  morning good morning dana well following  those shootings in uvalde and buffalo  lawmakers vowed to come together and  come up with common sense reform but the  longer it takes those senators to get  that deal to the floor for a vote the  longer its detractors have to pick the  legislation apart  as a teacher  i've imagined that scene in my own  classroom again and again  speaking to the national pta convention  friday first lady jill biden implored  congress to take action on gun control  we need to fight now for the lives of  our children and for the safety of our  schools this week a bipartisan group of  senators announced they'd agreed to a  basic framework of a deal including  enhanced background checks for gun  buyers under 21 and new funding for  school mental health and security  programs i'm more hopeful than ever  that we have a handle on all of the  issues  but lead republican negotiator john  cornyn had to defend the deal to a  hostile gop convention back home in  texas  but i will not  under any circumstance support new  restrictions for law abiding gun owners  that will always be my red line and some  republicans like fellow texan ted cruz  are already expressing concern about the  inclusion of so-called red flag laws  anyone that tries to take away our  second amendment rights i will stand and  fight to defend our liberties lead  democratic negotiator connecticut's  chris murphy says the group of senators  has committed to move forward with the  deal i have continued confidence that we  can  write that framework  into  into text and we can have that before  our colleagues next week  president biden has endorsed the  framework of this deal so has sent a  minority leader mitch mcconnell but  lawmakers still have to work out rules  about what they want to do there's a  provision that would ban domestic  abusers from buying guns they're also at  odds about what to do about sending  money to states that have red flag laws  that allow courts to confiscate guns  from people they believe pose a risk  michelle  a lot of work ahead christina thank you
 

